  "finding": "21r l.1-5 (62 signs, 16 groups) is in the sign set of 48r.8 and reads with the 48r key (solve_48r/key_48r_v2.json; decoded with that key unchanged it gives وانزادهارفعتهفاذكراسمربك?ينتاوي?ليهاوا?كرنعمهربكاذااستويتعليها, the ? being the two shapes not labelled in the 48r transcription: the horned EK, which takes ح in حين and ش in واشكر, and the squat alif W2) as the last third of the f. 21r rhymed prose, exactly where 48r.8 stops (after ربها جملته): 62 signs = 62 letters, 58 of 59 repeated-shape occurrences one letter per shape. It is the END of the 48r.8 cipher ('the fourth'), not a separate piece and not part of 20r.8. Against the clear text (وازدها نعمته ... اذا استوت بك عليها, 61 letters) the cipher reads وان زادها رفعته ... اذا استويت عليها (no بك). Slid ungapped along the whole 293-letter prose, the 48r-key decode matches 44 of 62 letters at the tail and at most 11 anywhere else.",
  "codicology": "So the top of f. 21r originally followed f. 48v (48v ends ربها جملته, 21r l.1 goes on وان زادها ...), and the compiler's فحللته سريعا لسهولته وهو on 21r l.6 is the solution of the fourth piece. This does not fit the quire-3-only model, which keeps 12v -> 21r: f. 21 (with 21v -> 22r continuous, so quire 4, ff. 21-28) also stood after f. 48. The joins 12v -> ? and 28v -> 49r (49r.1 begins mid-verse) need checking."
